        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "0a4bc9a2-249b-5f66-8532-2d7f6cd572cd",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Teams: LSU Tigers, Georgia Bulldogs, Oklahoma Sooners\n- Events: 2003 SEC Championship Game, 2004 Nokia Sugar Bowl, BCS national title game\n- Places: Louisiana Superdome, New Orleans, Louisiana\n- Topics: 2003 college football season, Bowl Championship Series\n\nFacts:\n- The LSU Tigers compiled an 11–1 regular season record in the 2003 college football season.\n- The LSU Tigers defeated the No. 5 Georgia Bulldogs in the 2003 SEC Championship Game after the regular season.\n- After winning the SEC Championship Game, the LSU Tigers were invited to play the Oklahoma Sooners in the Sugar Bowl for the Bowl Championship Series national title.\n- The 2004 Nokia Sugar Bowl was the BCS title game for the 2003 college football season.\n- The 2004 Nokia Sugar Bowl was played on January 4, 2004 at the Louisiana Superdome in New Orleans, Louisiana.",
